    correctAnswer: Tabon Caves, Palawan
    wrongAnswer1: Mayon Volcano, Albay
    wrongAnswer2: Banaue Rice Terraces
    wrongAnswer3: Fort Santiago, Manila
  - questionText: What was the main purpose of the Manunggul Jar?
    correctAnswer: Secondary burial
    wrongAnswer1: Cooking food
    wrongAnswer2: Transporting goods
    wrongAnswer3: Storing drinking water
  - questionText: What do the two human figures on the lid represent?
    correctAnswer: Souls traveling to the afterlife
    wrongAnswer1: Farmers planting rice
    wrongAnswer2: Warriors defending a village
    wrongAnswer3: Traders crossing the sea
  - questionText: Around which period does the Manunggul Jar date?
    correctAnswer: "890\u2013710 BC"
    wrongAnswer1: "1896\u20131898 AD"
    wrongAnswer2: "1941\u20131945 AD"
    wrongAnswer3: "1521\u20131565 AD"
  - questionText: In which country was the Manunggul Jar discovered?
    correctAnswer: Philippines
    wrongAnswer1: Indonesia
    wrongAnswer2: Thailand
    wrongAnswer3: Malaysia
